Load_Completion_Status: restore byte command and word coordinate stores

Original 0x44b873/0x44b87c stores X0 as WORD then code as BYTE. The
reconstructed DAT_0093de77 was int: assigning 0x38 after X0=64 cleared
bytes 0x93de78..0x93de7a, changing X0 to zero. Both ports painted an
extra black rectangle at x0..63/y416..439 during startup frames 10..19
(815 differing indexed pixels per frame against actual original Flips).
The second command is likewise BYTE (0x44b90e); all sixteen X/Y fields
are WORD stores at 0x44b873..0x44b8d1 and 0x44b8ed..0x44b940. Keep
the old-address aliases at the same widths. This restores packed PSX
primitive fields; it does not alter the original drawing algorithm.

